http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Chidanand Rajghatta</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134798850,imgsize-1185175.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Bryan Cranston rebuilt a $2.5M beach bungalow into a net-zero home, sold it for $5.45M]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134787193.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Bryan Cranston transformed a quaint beach bungalow into a stunning net-zero energy residence in Venice, California. The redesigned home showcases sleek modern aesthetics paired with cutting-edge sustainable energy solutions, reflecting eco-conscious principles. Listed in 2021, it achieved an impressive sale of $5.45 million, exceeding its initial purchase price. This remarkable project exemplifies the potential of sustainable living within today’s competitive real estate landscape.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2007-bryan-cranston-bought-a-california-beach-bungalow-for-2-5-million-after-rebuilding-it-as-a-2450-sq-ft-net-zero-energy-home-he-sold-the-property-14-years-later-for-5-45-million/articleshow/134787193.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2007-bryan-cranston-bought-a-california-beach-bungalow-for-2-5-million-after-rebuilding-it-as-a-2450-sq-ft-net-zero-energy-home-he-sold-the-property-14-years-later-for-5-45-million/articleshow/134787193.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-09T03:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134787355,imgsize-125389.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[New extinct crocodile found in Sphinx rocks, with a missing snout tip]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatim